<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal cabinet approves 3-year convergence plan.</title>
<headline>Portugal cabinet approves 3-year convergence plan.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese cabinet said it had approved a three-year plan for stability, growth and convergence with Europe's Economic and Monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>The cabinet said in a statement that it would present the 1998-2000 plan to parliament and the European Union on Friday.</p>
<p>The statement gave no further details.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Antonio Sousa Franco told Reuters last month that Portugal's budget deficit would be 2.0 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) in 1999 and might even be less this year than the forecast 2.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
